# Docker build context — what Railway (and any `docker build`) must upload.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# The Dockerfile begins `COPY . .`, and until now there was no .dockerignore, so
# the build context was the whole working tree: **209 GB**, of which 209 GB is
# `target/`. `.gitignore` does not apply to Docker, so a directory that git has
# correctly ignored since the first commit was still being packaged and shipped
# on every build.
#
#   before   209 GB
#   after    ~80 MB
#
# For a git-based deploy the context is a fresh checkout and `target/` is absent,
# so this file changes nothing there — it is insurance for every other path:
# `railway up`, a local `docker build`, or any CI runner with a warm target dir.
# In those cases the build does not fail with a useful error, it simply appears
# to hang while compressing a quarter-terabyte.
#
# ─── WHAT MUST NOT BE EXCLUDED ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Read this before adding a pattern. The Dockerfile needs more than it looks:
#
#   scripts/     NOT just shell scripts. Three [[bin]] targets live here, two of
#                which the Dockerfile builds by name:
#                  backfill-embedding-provenance = scripts/backfill_embedding_provenance.rs
#                  embedding-anchors             = scripts/embedding_anchors.rs
#                Excluding scripts/ breaks the build with a missing-path error.
#   migrations/  copied into the image; the api-server runs them at startup.
#   rabble-web/  copied to /app/static/rabble. Tracked in git precisely because
#                static/rabble is a build artifact and is gitignored.
#   agents/ apps/ ontologies/ templates/ static/   all copied into the runtime image.
#   crates/      fermi-console is stripped from the workspace by sed, not by
#                absence — the path must still exist for Cargo.toml to parse
#                before sed runs.
#   Cargo.lock   a release build must not silently resolve different versions
#                than the ones tested.

# ─── The 209 GB ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/target/

# ─── Version control ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 180 MB, and the build reads no git metadata. Note: if a future build wants to
# stamp a commit into /api/health from git rather than an env var, this line is
# what makes that impossible — pass it as a build arg instead.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ─── Documentation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 43 MB, mostly PDFs. Nothing reads docs/ at runtime.
docs/
*.pdf
*.md
!README.md

# ─── CI / editor / OS cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.zed/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# ─── Local-only state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets must reach the container as Railway variables, never baked into a
# layer: anything copied in is readable by anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Created by the Dockerfile itself (`mkdir -p /app/avatars_cache`).
avatars_cache/

# Flutter build output. The Dockerfile copies rabble-web/ to this path inside the
# image instead, so shipping a local copy is wasted bytes that would be
# overwritten anyway.
static/rabble/

# Test and coverage artifacts
tarpaulin-report.html
cobertura.xml
*.profraw
